            <Placemark id="2044">
                <name>House of Windsor (old cigar factory) - roof torn off / partial collapse (York Township (Yoe / Dallastown), PA)</name>
                <description>Social Media | has contact: Yes
NEW this report
storm damage to commercial/industrial roof (wind - roof torn off, partial collapse) | Open - storm-damaged roof | 2026-11-26 (WGAL story updated 3:50 PM EST; CBS 21 WHP story 12:47 PM, updated 9:59 PM EST)
Thanksgiving nor'easter winds tore the roof off and caused a partial collapse of a building in the 100 block of Orchard Street, York Township PA, around 10:30 AM 11/26; everyone out, no injuries; Advanced Technical Rescue Team stabilizing the building. CBS 21: the building is the old House of Windsor cigar manufacturing company.
Contact: House of Windsor Inc (directory listing)
Phone: (717) 244-4501
Email: -
Can solicit: Yes (No state license)
No state license for commercial roofing; check city/county rules (general info, not legal advice)
Website: -
Confidence: Low-Medium (business directory listing only; building may no longer be an active factory - confirm owner before any outreach)
Source: https://www.wgal.com/article/orchard-street-building-collapse-york-township/74542854 ; https://local21news.com/news/local/strong-storms-rip-roof-off-of-home-in-york-county-dispatch-noreaster-wind-rain-house-thanksgiving
~1014 mi from Omaha</description>
